# Timber - ten woodwinds, levelled but not yet voiced by ear.
#
# What has been done here is the *machine* and the *balance*. What has not is
# whether each of these sounds like the instrument on the label; that is Dan's
# ear against the debug build.
#
# **Levelled to about -23 dB RMS.** The spread was 15.0 dB and is 3.8: every
# patch carried the default volume, so Stopped Wood sat 15 dB over the Oboe.
# Init is the only one left outside, 3 dB under, and it has to be - an Init
# sets nothing by rule, so it is the machine's own default and not a choice.
# Oboe is at 1.49 of a maximum 1.5 and has nothing left; if it ever needs more
# it has to come from pressure or reed rather than from the fader.
#
# **Two hard gates were fixed in the machine** (see the commit): the tongue
# came off the reed in one sample, and the key click stopped dead with its
# filter still ringing. Worst second-difference score against the local level:
# Init 4.93 to 2.30, Clarinet 4.95 to 2.36, Bass Clarinet 4.53 to 2.80, Oboe
# 4.00 to 2.56, Bassoon 4.48 to 2.65.
#
# **This machine does not have the brass one's fault.** Measured as the first
# pass down the tube against the settled tone - the thing that found four
# faults in Brazen - the clarinet reads 0.4x, 0.6x and 1.0x across the bands
# where the tuba read 24.7x. Timber's tube is short and its output is gated by
# the envelope, so there is no unfiltered first pass to hear.
#
# **The `edge` column stays high, 5x to 14x, and it is the breath.** Not the
# key click, which was the obvious guess and is wrong: Stopped Wood reads
# 14.3x with `keys` at 0.45 and 14.3x with it at zero. With `breath` at zero
# it reads 7.2x. Breath noise is broadband and the settled tone is not, so any
# patch with air in it measures an onset brighter than its body - which is
# what a woodwind is. Left alone deliberately. The noise is white to Nyquist,
# which no airstream is, and tilting it the way the brass's was tilted would
# halve this number; it would also take the air out of the flute and the pan
# pipe, which is most of what they are. That is a tone decision and wants an
# ear, not a measurement.
#
# **They play flat**, -3 to -17 cents, worst on the bass clarinet. That is the
# machine and it predates this work - the plan's own section records the
# clarinet at -10.4 cents as measured. Not addressed here.
#
# Forked's pitch column reads about -4100 cents. That is the measurement, not
# the patch: a fork fingering deliberately sits between two modes and the F0
# finder cannot follow it.
#
# Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Timber` lists
# them. A patch names only what it changes.

machine Timber
# A melody rather than one held note: one note is what one note sounds
# like, and a bank can pass that patch by patch and still be the same
# sound all the way down.
role    tune

patch Init

patch Clarinet
  attack         0.02 s
  breath         0.1
  keys           0.2

  volume         1.17
patch "Bass Clarinet"
  body           73.4 Hz
  breath         0.16
  embouchure     0.5
  keys           0.35
  lattice        1000 Hz
  pressure       0.9
  tongue         0.6

  volume         0.95
patch "Alto Sax"
  attack         0.015 s
  body           138.6 Hz
  bore           #1
  breath         0.2
  embouchure     0.5
  keys           0.3
  lattice        900 Hz
  pressure       0.95
  tongue         0.75
  vibrato        9 cents

  volume         0.93
patch Oboe
  attack         0.012 s
  body           233.1 Hz
  bore           #1
  breath         0.08
  embouchure     0.7
  family         #1
  keys           0.2
  lattice        1600 Hz
  pressure       0.95
  tongue         0.8
  vibrato        12 cents

  volume         1.49
patch Bassoon
  attack         0.025 s
  body           58.3 Hz
  bore           #1
  embouchure     0.6
  family         #1
  keys           0.4
  lattice        700 Hz
  pressure       0.9

  volume         0.93
patch Flute
  attack         0.04 s
  body           261.6 Hz
  bore           #1
  breath         0.45
  family         #2
  keys           0.15
  lattice        1400 Hz
  pressure       0.8
  tongue         0.35
  vibrato        10.8 cents

  volume         0.67
patch "Pan Pipe"
  aim            0.1
  attack         0.06 s
  body           196 Hz
  breath         0.6
  family         #2
  jet            0.55
  lattice        2200 Hz
  pressure       0.7
  tongue         0.2

  volume         0.86
patch "Stopped Wood"
  answer         0.385
  attack         0.05 s
  body           110 Hz
  breath         0.3
  drive          0.2
  embouchure     0.45
  holes          0.9
  lattice        420 Hz
  pressure       1
  tongue         0.5

  volume         0.26
patch Forked
  answer         0.4675
  attack         0.04 s
  below          1.74
  bore           #1
  breath         0.25
  embouchure     0.5
  family         #1
  fingering      0.8
  flutter        0.35
  lattice        1200 Hz
  pressure       1
  tongue         0.6

  volume         0.83